# UNIT TESTS -- THE 31 FAILURES THIS PATCH CAUSED, AND THE FIX  (LW-M4-14)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The version of this patch that landed for LW-M4-10 broke 31 Fenix unit tests, and
# its report did not mention unit tests at all. That is the second time this exact
# casualty class shipped -- LW-M4-03 broke five in NimbusSystemTest and LW-M4-13
# exists to clean it up -- so docs/android/AGENTS.md now names
# `./mach gradle fenix:testDebugUnitTest` in the definition of done for any
# Kotlin-layer patch. A Gradle build compiling is not its tests passing: the combined
# build these numbers come from had exit 0 from both `mach build` and
# `gradle assembleDebug` while 31 tests were red.
#
# MEASURED, all android patches applied, `./mach gradle fenix:testDebugUnitTest
# --continue` over the six affected classes: 188 tests, 31 failed. Per class, and
# every one of the 31 an assertion failure -- code that ran and disagreed, not a
# compile error and not the environment:
#
#   ContentRecommendationsFeatureHelperTest   16   the per-locale matrix
#   ReviewPromptMiddlewareTest                 8   the trigger arithmetic
#   ContinuousOnboardingFeatureTest            3   day-2/3/7 gating
#   SettingsTest                               2   shouldShowOnboarding
#   PocketMiddlewareTest                       1   StartAction schedules the workers
#   TermsOfUsePromptRepositoryTest             1   "all conditions satisfied"
#
# Every one of the 31 asserted the behaviour this patch removes, so the fix is not to
# weaken the patch: it is to make the tests assert the NEW behaviour. That is worth
# more than the originals were. These are the assertions an upstream rebase has to
# break to bring onboarding, the stories carousel, the review prompt or the Terms of
# Use sheet back, and there is now a red test waiting for each.
#
# What changed, file by file, and the one place tests were deleted rather than
# inverted:
#
#   SettingsTest              2 inverted (a feature-enabled first run, and the Secret
#     Settings enablePersistentOnboarding escape hatch that forced the flow on every
#     HomeActivity creation regardless of the flag) + 1 ADDED that calls
#     shouldShowOnboarding with no featureEnabled argument, so the default parameter
#     is exercised as well. That default is Settings.onboardingFeatureEnabled, itself
#     initialised from FeatureFlags.ONBOARDING_FEATURE_ENABLED, so the new test pins
#     the compiled constant on every channel -- not only on the debug build where
#     upstream's `!Config.channel.isDebug` already made it false.
#   ContinuousOnboardingFeatureTest   3 inverted, setup kept verbatim: each still
#     sets continuousOnboardingFeatureEnabled = true, which is what keeps the
#     assertion non-vacuous.
#   TermsOfUsePromptRepositoryTest    1 inverted, setup and its three sanity
#     assertions kept verbatim -- they prove every upstream condition really is
#     satisfied (settings.isTermsOfUsePromptEnabled included) and the answer is still
#     no.
#   PocketMiddlewareTest      1 inverted to verify(exactly = 0), still constructed
#     with FakePocketSettings() and its `true` defaults, so it asserts that the
#     schedulers stay unreachable even when the settings ask for them + 1 ADDED for
#     SettingsBackedPocketSettings, which upstream never tested and which is the
#     SECOND path into the same two fetches: its showPocketRecommendationsFeature
#     used to OR in settings.privateModeAndStoriesEntryPointEnabled, which the FML
#     enables on the developer and nightly channels. The new test answers true to all
#     three backing settings through a mock and requires both overrides to stay false.
#   ContentRecommendationsFeatureHelperTest   18 tests -> 4. The only file where a
#     per-test inversion would have been eighteen copies of "false is false". Both
#     helpers are unconditional now, so the replacement loops over the same fourteen
#     locale tags the deleted tests covered and requires both helpers to stay false in
#     every one, plus the two unsupported-locale tests kept as they were. The tag list
#     is a literal in the test and deliberately NOT a read of
#     CONTENT_RECOMMENDATIONS_SUPPORTED_LOCALE: a loop over the production constant
#     would still pass if a rebase reinstated the locale check and shrank the list.
#   ReviewPromptMiddlewareTest   10 tests -> 6. Eight asserted that a satisfied
#     trigger makes the app Eligible; two asserted that criteria evaluation
#     short-circuits. handleReviewPromptCheck evaluates nothing at all now, so the
#     short-circuit pair had nothing left to assert and is DELETED -- subsumed by the
#     two new "no criterion is evaluated" tests, which are strictly stronger (nothing
#     is evaluated, so nothing can continue past anything). The other four new tests
#     are "every criterion satisfied, still NotEligible", one per combination of
#     trigger mode and custom-prompt setting. The JEXL half needs no assertion of its
#     own: the file's createJexlHelper fake answers assertUnused() to every method, so
#     an evaluated expression fails the test wherever it happens.
