# One thing LW-M4-14 changed in the production hunks, and why
# ----------------------------------------------------------
# `mach gradle fenix:ktlint` was RED on the landed version, in this patch's own file:
#
#   FeatureFlags.kt:36:15: Property name should use the screaming snake case notation
#   when the value can not be changed (standard:property-naming)
#
# Making the flag `const` is what folds it into every call site, and `const val`
# requires SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE -- which is what its three neighbours in the same
# object already use (PULL_TO_REFRESH_ENABLED, FX_SUGGEST, FIREFOX_LABS); upstream's
# camelCase name was legal only because upstream's declaration was not `const`. So
# the flag is renamed to `ONBOARDING_FEATURE_ENABLED`, which touches exactly one more
# line -- Settings.kt's `var onboardingFeatureEnabled = FeatureFlags.<flag>`, in a
# file this patch already edits. Nothing else in the tree reads the FeatureFlags
# constant: the androidTest helpers all read Settings.onboardingFeatureEnabled, whose
# name is unchanged, and the two remaining textual mentions are KDoc code samples in
# components/settings/FeatureFlagPreference.kt (a file this patch does not own and
# whose behaviour does not depend on the name).
# The compiled shape is unchanged by the rename, measured with javap on the class the
# unit-test run compiled rather than inferred:
#   public static final boolean ONBOARDING_FEATURE_ENABLED = false;
# with the constant inlined and NO accessor emitted -- the only getter in the class is
# getCustomExtensionCollectionFeature(), for the one property that is not `const`.
